# oracle: compute voronoi/atom neighbors yes (local array) in a 3x3x3 simple cubic box periodic in x and y and fixed in z: the exterior faces at the z walls are native's (row order and face neighbour zero)
# Measured (ORACLE_MEASURE=1): thermo 1.8e-15; the local rows (boundary p p f: exterior faces of the z walls, neighbour 0) agree at 1e-12 (filerel); engine ~0.1 s warm. native: lmp b332f28, sort off.
# oracle-files: w199vo_mixed.loc
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=none rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10 filerel=1e-12
units           lj
atom_style      atomic
atom_modify     map array sort 0 0.0
boundary        p p f
lattice         sc 1.0
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0
pair_style      lj/cut 1.5
pair_coeff      * * 1.0 1.0
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
compute         v all voronoi/atom neighbors yes
dump            d all local 1 w199vo_mixed.loc c_v[1] c_v[2] c_v[3]
dump_modify     d format float %.15g
run             0
undump          d
